    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0167" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.24/60</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-12T01:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1918,
                                1 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 16, 10.22
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>89. Daily reports that Germans rapidly making purchases, and that German
                    purchasing commission will arrive within a few days. <pb facs="0168" n="118"
                        xml:id="pg118"/> Military attaché joins me in recommending that purchase of
                    such supplies be assigned to Consul General at Moscow as civilian committee
                    making little headway. Such purchases should be made without delay and assembled
                    at Archangel. Consul General is familiar with matter and can engage competent
                    men therefor. I shall cooperate with him if you desire. See my Nos. 50 and
                    44.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
